        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1768279188304",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768279188305_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a concise, executive-ready account insight explaining why this account should be prioritized.\n\nHard Constraint:\nOutput must be 900 characters or fewer, including spaces.\nKey Reasons must have 3 points, and Risk Analysis must have 2 points.\n\n  Use the following data sources:\n  - Account details: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAIL.$output}}\n  - Product intelligence: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_PRODUCT_INTELLIGENCES.$output}}\n  - Opportunities: {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITIES_BY_ACCOUNT.$output}}\n  - Product footprint: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_FOOTPRINT.$output}}\n\n  Start with a single sentence summarizing why the account should be prioritized now. Then provide the key supporting reasons as bullet points, include a separate Risk Analysis section, and conclude with a recommended next action.\n\n  If Strategy = Cross-Sell:\n  Explain why the account is a strong cross-sell opportunity. Use Demand Stage signals such as Awareness, Consideration, or Sales Ready, along with Product Fit, Buying Group Coverage %, Buying Group Engagement %, and any open opportunity for the Target Product. Add relevant context from Product Footprint, recent opportunities, Buying Group stakeholder engagement activity, and other account-level data available on the page.\n\n  If Strategy = Renewal:\n  Explain whether the account is Critical Risk, High Risk, Moderate Risk, or Stable. Support the assessment using Product Risk, Usage, Satisfaction, Renewal Timing, Support Signals, Buying Group Coverage, and Buying Group Engagement. Explicitly use the riskDetailedExplainer field from Product Intelligence, when explaining renewal risk drivers. Add relevant context from Product Footprint, recent opportunities, Buying Group stakeholder engagement activity, and other account-level data available on the page.\n\n  Risk Analysis:\n  Include a dedicated Risk Analysis section after the key supporting reasons. Use Product Intelligence data, especially the riskDetailedExplainer field, to explain the most important risk drivers by product when available. Mention the affected product names, risk classification, usage or adoption concerns, renewal timing, support or satisfaction signals, and why these risks matter to the current account strategy. If no meaningful risk signals are available, state that no material risk signals are evident from the available data.\n\n  If no Strategy is provided:\n  Generate a neutral account summary using the strongest available signals across account details, product footprint, product intelligence, opportunities, engagement, usage, satisfaction, and risk.\n\n  Guidelines:\n  - Keep the response concise and business-focused.\n  - Use only the available data; do not invent missing metrics or facts.\n  - Prioritize the strongest signals over listing every available detail.\n  - Make the recommended next action specific to the account’s current status.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7502,
            "y": 6370
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Footprint Display"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_FOOTPRINT_DISPLAY",
          "id": "1768257610425",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768257610427_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a multiRecordWidget with columns: \"Product Name\", \"Status\", \"Stage\", \"ARR\", \"Renewal Date\", \"Usage Level\", \"Risk Classification\" based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_PRODUCT_INTELLIGENCES.$output.items}}.\n\n\"Product Name\" -> productName, \n\"Status\" -> <Remove ORA_ from ownershipStatus and Generate a proper Init Caps text and represent as a badge based on its value>, \n\"Stage\" -> implementationStage (represent as a badge and assign priority based on the value), \n\"ARR\" -> arr formatted using K for thousands, M for millions, and B for billions with exactly two decimal places and no space before the suffix. Examples: 2,100,000 -> 2.10M; 2,123,000 -> 2.12M; 2,127,000 -> 2.13M,\n\"Renewal Date\" -> renewalDate, \n\"Usage Level\" -> usageLevel, \n\"Risk Classification\" -> riskClassification \n\nWhen generating the response, do not use ALL CAPS for words, sentences, headings, or labels.\nUse normal sentence case or title case only.\nAvoid fully capitalized words unless they are part of a proper noun that is normally written in uppercase.\n\nReturn only the top 6 rows.\n\nUse {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_DETAIL.$output}}, {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_PRODUCT_INTELLIGENCES.$output}},{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_FOOTPRINT.$output}} to generate content for the following fields.\n\nTitle : \"[Account Name]'s subscriptions\"\nDescription : Place this immediately after the widget title and before the multiRecordWidget table. Generate a concise 2–3 sentence executive summary. Explicitly mention the company name and the specific products being discussed when available in the data. Start by summarizing the company’s product footprint, adoption strength, and risk posture. Then identify the most relevant renewal, lifecycle, usage, or product-footprint signal that creates a strategic sales entry point. Conclude by recommending how to position the named target product or next sales play. If the strategy is Cross-Sell, frame named existing products, upcoming renewals, high-usage areas, or lifecycle events as entry points for expansion into the named target product. If the strategy is Renewal, frame named product health, adoption, risk, and renewal timing as the basis for retention, adoption improvement, or expansion. Keep the language business-oriented, specific, and grounded only in the available account, product intelligence, footprint, and opportunity data. Do not use generic references such as \"the account,\" \"this customer,\" \"existing products,\" or \"target product\" when company or product names are available."
            },
            {
              "id": "1768257610425_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Must output only the multiRecordWidget. No other text.\nDo not include the widget title and widget description"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6065,
            "y": 6592
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Account Subtitle"
          },
          "outcomes": {
