            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Opportunity Display"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_OPPORTUNITY_DISPLAY",
          "id": "1778743328242",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778743328242_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Must output only the multiRecordWidget. No other text.\nDo not include the widget title and widget description"
            },
            {
              "id": "1778743328242_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a multiRecordWidget with columns: \"Opportunity Type\", \"Product\", \"Opportunity Name\", \"Opportunity Status\", \"Stage\", \"Creation Date\" based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITIES_BY_ACCOUNT.$output}}.\n\n\"Opportunity Type\" -> <Generate a proper Initcaps English text based on type. represent as a badge and assign priority based on the value)>,\n\"Product\" -> <For each object in the top-level items array:\n1. Extract all values from revenueLines.items[*].accountProductIntelligence.productName\n2. Join the product names into a single comma-delimited string named productNames, If the concatenated productNames string exceeds 100 characters, truncate it to the first 100 characters and append 3 dots\n3. If revenueLines.items is empty, return an empty string>,\n  \"Opportunity Name\" -> name,\n  \"Opportunity Status\" -> <Generate a proper Initcaps English text based on status. represent as a badge and assign priority based on the\n  value)>,\n  \"Stage\" -> salesStage,\n  \"Creation Date\" - <Get the data part with out the time part from opportunityCreationDate. For example, 2026-01-25T12:37:47.383Z should\n  represent as 2026-01-25>\n\n  When generating the response, do not use ALL CAPS for words, sentences, headings, or labels.\n  Use normal sentence case or title case only.\n  Avoid fully capitalized words unless they are part of a proper noun that is normally written in uppercase.\n\n  Title : Generate a concise, business-oriented heading that summarizes the strategic value of the current opportunities. The title should reference account momentum, expansion potential, renewal readiness, or pipeline strength when supported by the data. Avoid generic phrasing such as \"how existing opportunities support the account strategy\" or \"for target product.\" Keep it natural, specific, and executive-friendly.\n\n  Description : Generate a 2–3 sentence executive summary explaining how the account’s existing opportunities support the current strategy for the target product. Explicitly mention the account name and the specific products being discussed when available in the data. Use the widget data to identify account momentum, active sales motions, business priorities, opportunity stage, renewal or expansion signals, and sales readiness. Explain how the named opportunities can be used to position the named target product, strengthen stakeholder alignment, and accelerate either cross-sell or renewal outcomes. Keep the language strategic, business-oriented, and grounded only in the available opportunity and account data. Do not use generic references such as \"the account,\" \"this customer,\" \"existing opportunities,\" or \"target product\" when account or product names are available.\n\nReturn only the top 5 rows.\n\n  Widget structure requirements:\n  - Put the generated title in the widget's root title field.\n  - Put the generated executive summary in the widget's root description field.\n  - The description must appear immediately after the title and before the multiRecordWidget table.\n  - Do not place the description after the widget.\n  - Do not generate any prose outside the widget.\n  - Return only the completed widget.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6515,
            "y": 6592
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
